Both Basic Auth and Preemptive Auth use the same authentication mechanism — HTTP Basic Authentication
(i.e., sending username and password in a Base64-encoded format in the Authorization header).

🔄 The only difference is when the credentials are sent:
| Auth Type           | Sends Credentials Immediately? | Requires 401 First? | Number of Requests           |
| ------------------- | ------------------------------ | ------------------- | ---------------------------- |
| **Basic Auth**      | ❌ No                           | ✅ Yes               | 2 requests (initial + retry) |
| **Preemptive Auth** | ✅ Yes                          | ❌ No                | 1 request                    |

//non preemptive auth
given()
    .auth()
    .basic("user", "pass") // Server may respond 401 first

//preemptive auth
given()
    .auth()
    .preemptive()
    .basic("user", "pass") // Sends credentials immediately


for passing bearer token in header we should pass like below:

 * given()
 *     .header("Authorization", "Bearer your_actual_token_here")
 *     .when()
 *     .get("/api/protected-resource")
 *     .then()
 *     .statusCode(200);


| Auth Type       | Method / Syntax                              |
| --------------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| Basic Auth      | `.auth().basic()`                            |
| Preemptive Auth | `.auth().preemptive().basic()`               |
| Digest Auth     | `.auth().digest()`                           |
| OAuth 1.0       | `.auth().oauth()`                            |
| OAuth 2.0       | `.auth().oauth2()` or Bearer header          |
| API Key         | `.header("x-api-key", "key")` or query param |


